{"type":"message","id":"73f93aef","parentId":"45ecf9a8","timestamp":"2026-03-08T10:13:16.784Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Sun 2026-03-08 11:13 GMT+1] Analyze OpenClaw's batch memory storage feature implementation.\n\n## Current Implementation\n\nI have a neuro-memory bridge that stores events to a Python MCP server. Currently, EVERY `emit()` call immediately triggers `storeToNeuroMemory()` which calls the Python process.\n\n### Code Files\n\n**neuro-memory-bridge.ts** (MCP protocol bridge):\n- `storeMemory()` sends JSON request to Python process via stdin\n- Uses method-specific timeouts (store_memory: 60s timeout)\n- Each call is synchronous - waits for Python response\n- Python process is spawned once at startup\n\n**event-mesh.ts** (Event bus wired to neuro-memory):\n- `emit()` method calls `storeToNeuroMemory()` for memorable events\n- Check `isMemorable()` filters out noisy events (heartbeat, ping, etc)\n- Store is fire-and-forget (async, non-blocking)\n- But underlying `neuroMemory.storeMemory()` still calls Python synchronously\n\n### The Problem\n\nDuring high activity (e.g., tool execution burst), we get:\n1. Multiple `emit()` calls in quick succession\n2. Each triggers `storeMemory()` → Python IPC call\n3. Python process gets overwhelmed with sequential requests\n4. Timeouts occur (60s limit)\n\n### Proposed Solution: Batch Memory Storage\n\nAdd batching with debouncing:\n1. Queue memory operations in TypeScript\n2. Flush when queue reaches N items OR after X milliseconds\n3. Send batch to Python in single request\n4. Reduce Python IPC overhead by 10-100x\n\n## Your Analysis Task\n\nPlease analyze:\n\n1. **Current wiring** - Trace the exact flow from `emit()` to Python IPC\n2. **Batch implementation** - Where to add batching logic?\n3. **Edge cases** - What happens if:\n   - Queue fills up during burst?\n   - Python process crashes mid-batch?\n   - Gateway restarts with queued memories?\n4. **Implementation steps** - Specific code changes needed\n5. **Performance estimate** - Expected improvement (N IPC calls → 1 batch call)\n\nProvide actual TypeScript code snippets for the batch queue implementation."}],"timestamp":1772964796783}}
