{"type":"message","id":"93126523","parentId":"d0e912c4","timestamp":"2026-03-08T10:15:36.068Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a complete understanding of the codebase. Let me compile my analysis with TypeScript code snippets for the batch implementation.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete picture. Let me provide a comprehensive analysis.\n\n---\n\n## Batch Memory Storage Analysis\n\n### 1. Current Wiring - Flow from `emit()` to Python IPC\n\n```\nUser Code / Tool Execution\n       │\n       ▼\nAgentEventMesh.emit(event)\n       │\n       ├─► Add to history (in-memory)\n       │\n       ├─► persistEvent() (SQLite, async)\n       │\n       ├─► bus.emit() (EventEmitter)\n       │\n       └─► isMemorable(event)?\n              │ YES\n              ▼\n           storeToNeuroMemory(event)     [event-mesh.ts:252]\n              │ fire-and-forget (non-blocking)\n              ▼\n           neuroMemory.storeMemory(content, metadata)  [neuro-memory-bridge.ts:111]\n              │ SYNCHRONOUS - awaits response\n              ▼\n           request(\"store_memory\", {...})  [neuro-memory-bridge.ts:205]\n              │\n              ├─► JSON.stringify({id, method, params})\n              │\n              ├─► process.stdin.write(json + \"\\n\")\n              │\n              └─► await Promise (60s timeout)\n                     │\n                     ▼\n              Python MCP Server (mcp_server.py)\n                     │\n                     └─► Response via stdout\n                            │\n                            ▼\n                   processBuffer() → resolve/reject\n```\n\n**Key Problem**: While `storeToNeuroMemory()` is fire-and-forget at the event-mesh level, the underlying `request()` call in `NeuroMemoryBridge` is **synchronous** - it awaits the Python response. During a tool execution burst:\n- 10 events → 10 sequential IPC calls → 10 JSON serializations → 10 Python roundtrips\n- Each call has 60s timeout but typically takes 100-500ms\n- Total latency: 1-5 seconds for 10 events (sequential processing)\n\n### 2. Batch Implementation Location\n\nThe **optimal location** for batching is in **`neuro-memory-bridge.ts`**, NOT in `event-mesh.ts`. Here's why:\n\n| Location | Pros | Cons |\n|----------|------|------|\n| **event-mesh.ts** | Simple add-on | Couples batching to event logic; can't batch direct calls |\n| **neuro-memory-bridge.ts** ✓ | Transparent to callers; batches all sources | Slightly more complex |\n\nAdd a `MemoryBatchQueue` class similar to the existing `MetricsQueue` pattern.\n\n### 3. TypeScript Implementation\n\n```typescript\n// ============================================================\n// FILE: src/agents/memory-batch-queue.ts\n// ============================================================\n\nimport { randomUUID } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport { createSubsystemLogger } from \"../logging/subsystem.js\";\n\nconst log = createSubsystemLogger(\"memory-batch\");\n\nexport type BatchMemoryItem = {\n  id: string;\n  content: string;\n  metadata?: Record<string, unknown>;\n  embedding?: number[];\n};\n\nexport type BatchStoreResult = {\n  id: string;\n  result: {\n    stored: boolean;\n    episode_id?: string;\n    surprise: number;\n    is_novel: boolean;\n    reason?: string;\n  };\n};\n\nexport interface MemoryBatchConfig {\n  /** Max items before flush - default: 10 */\n  batchSize?: number;\n  /** Max wait time before flush (ms) - default: 2000 (2 seconds) */\n  flushInterval?: number;\n  /** Max queue size before drop oldest - default: 100 */\n  maxQueueSize?: number;\n  /** Callback to send batch to Python */\n  onFlush: (items: BatchMemoryItem[]) => Promise<BatchStoreResult[]>;\n}\n\nexport class MemoryBatchQueue {\n  private buffer: BatchMemoryItem[] = [];\n  private flushTimer?: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout>;\n  private readonly batchSize: number;\n  private readonly flushInterval: number;\n  private readonly maxQueueSize: number;\n  private readonly onFlush: (items: BatchMemoryItem[]) => Promise<BatchStoreResult[]>;\n  \n  private isFlushing = false;\n  private pendingCallbacks: Map<string, {\n    resolve: (result: BatchStoreResult['result']) => void;\n    reject: (error: Error) => void;\n  }> = new Map();\n  \n  private totalStored = 0;\n  private totalDropped = 0;\n\n  constructor(config: MemoryBatchConfig) {\n    this.batchSize = config.batchSize ?? 10;\n    this.flushInterval = config.flushInterval ?? 2000;\n    this.maxQueueSize = config.maxQueueSize ?? 100;\n    this.onFlush = config.onFlush;\n    \n    this.startFlushTimer();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Add memory to batch queue (non-blocking, <0.1ms)\n   * Returns a promise that resolves when the batch is flushed\n   */\n  push(item: Omit<BatchMemoryItem, 'id'>): Promise<BatchStoreResult['result']> {\n    const id = randomUUID();\n    const fullItem: BatchMemoryItem = { ...item, id };\n    \n    // Enforce max queue size (drop oldest if overflow)\n    if (this.buffer.length >= this.maxQueueSize) {\n      const dropped = this.buffer.shift();\n      if (dropped) {\n        const callback = this.pendingCallbacks.get(dropped.id);\n        if (callback) {\n          this.pendingCallbacks.delete(dropped.id);\n          callback.reject(new Error(\"Memory dropped due to queue overflow\"));\n        }\n        this.totalDropped++;\n        log.warn(`Memory queue overflow, dropped item: ${dropped.id}`);\n      }\n    }\n    \n    this.buffer.push(fullItem);\n    \n    // Create promise for this item's result\n    const resultPromise = new Promise<BatchStoreResult['result']>((resolve, reject) => {\n      this.pendingCallbacks.set(id, { resolve, reject });\n    });\n    \n    // Flush immediately if batch full\n    if (this.buffer.length >= this.batchSize) {\n      this.scheduleFlush();\n    }\n    \n    return resultPromise;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Force flush all pending items\n   */\n  async flush(): Promise<void> {\n    if (this.isFlushing || this.buffer.length === 0) return;\n    \n    this.isFlushing = true;\n    \n    // Swap buffer atomically\n    const toProcess = [...this.buffer];\n    this.buffer = [];\n    \n    log.debug(`Flushing ${toProcess.length} memory items`);\n    \n    try {\n      const results = await this.onFlush(toProcess);\n      \n      // Dispatch results to waiting callers\n      for (const result of results) {\n        const callback = this.pendingCallbacks.get(result.id);\n        if (callback) {\n          this.pendingCallbacks.delete(result.id);\n          if (result.result.stored) {\n            this.totalStored++;\n          }\n          callback.resolve(result.result);\n        }\n      }\n      \n      // Reject any items that didn't get results (Python error)\n      for (const item of toProcess) {\n        if (this.pendingCallbacks.has(item.id)) {\n          const callback = this.pendingCallbacks.get(item.id)!;\n          this.pendingCallbacks.delete(item.id);\n          callback.reject(new Error(\"No result returned from batch store\"));\n        }\n      }\n      \n    } catch (error) {\n      // Batch failed - reject all pending\n      const msg = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);\n      log.error(`Batch flush failed: ${msg}`);\n      \n      for (const item of toProcess) {\n        const callback = this.pendingCallbacks.get(item.id);\n        if (callback) {\n          this.pendingCallbacks.delete(item.id);\n          callback.reject(new Error(`Batch failed: ${msg}`));\n        }\n      }\n    } finally {\n      this.isFlushing = false;\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get current queue statistics\n   */\n  getStats() {\n    return {\n      queueSize: this.buffer.length,\n      pendingCallbacks: this.pendingCallbacks.size,\n      totalStored: this.totalStored,\n      totalDropped: this.totalDropped,\n      isFlushing: this.isFlushing,\n    };\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Stop timer and flush remaining\n   */\n  async shutdown(): Promise<void> {\n    if (this.flushTimer) {\n      clearTimeout(this.flushTimer);\n      this.flushTimer = undefined;\n    }\n    await this.flush();\n  }\n\n  private scheduleFlush(): void {\n    // Immediate flush via setImmediate (doesn't block current call)\n    setImmediate(() => this.flush());\n  }\n\n  private startFlushTimer(): void {\n    this.flushTimer = setInterval(() => {\n      if (this.buffer.length > 0) {\n        this.flush();\n      }\n    }, this.flushInterval);\n    \n    // Don't prevent process exit\n    if (this.flushTimer.unref) {\n      this.flushTimer.unref();\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Modified `neuro-memory-bridge.ts`\n\n```typescript\n// ============================================================\n// MODIFICATIONS TO: src/agents/neuro-memory-bridge.ts\n// ============================================================\n\nimport { MemoryBatchQueue, type BatchMemoryItem, type BatchStoreResult } from \"./memory-batch-queue.js\";\n\nexport class NeuroMemoryBridge {\n  private process: ChildProcess | null = null;\n  private config: NeuroMemoryConfig;\n  private requestCallbacks: Map<string, { resolve: Function; reject: Function }> = new Map();\n  private requestId = 0;\n  private buffer = \"\";\n  private isReady = false;\n  private consolidateTimer?: ReturnType<typeof setInterval>;\n  \n  // NEW: Batch queue for memory operations\n  private memoryBatch?: MemoryBatchQueue;\n\n  constructor(config: NeuroMemoryConfig) {\n    this.config = {\n      pythonPath: config.pythonPath || \"python3\",\n      inputDim: config.inputDim || 768,\n      autoConsolidate: config.autoConsolidate ?? true,\n      consolidateIntervalMs: config.consolidateIntervalMs || 3600000,\n      // NEW: Batching config\n      enableBatching: config.enableBatching ?? true,\n      batchConfig: {\n        batchSize: config.batchConfig?.batchSize ?? 10,\n        flushInterval: config.batchConfig?.flushInterval ?? 2000,\n        maxQueueSize: config.batchConfig?.maxQueueSize ?? 100,\n        ...config.batchConfig,\n      },\n      ...config,\n    };\n  }\n\n  async start(): Promise<void> {\n    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      // ... existing spawn logic ...\n      \n      this.process = spawn(this.config.pythonPath!, [`${this.config.agentPath}/mcp_server.py`], {\n        cwd: this.config.agentPath,\n        stdio: [\"pipe\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"],\n      });\n\n      // ... existing error/exit handlers ...\n\n      this.process.stderr?.on(\"data\", (data) => {\n        const msg = data.toString().trim();\n        if (msg.includes(\"MCP Server started\")) {\n          this.isReady = true;\n          \n          // NEW: Initialize batch queue\n          if (this.config.enableBatching) {\n            this.initBatchQueue();\n          }\n          \n          log.info(\"✅ Neuro-memory-agent MCP server ready\");\n          \n          if (this.config.autoConsolidate) {\n            this.startAutoConsolidation();\n          }\n          resolve();\n        }\n      });\n      \n      // ... rest of start logic ...\n    });\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * NEW: Initialize batch queue\n   */\n  private initBatchQueue(): void {\n    this.memoryBatch = new MemoryBatchQueue({\n      batchSize: this.config.batchConfig!.batchSize,\n      flushInterval: this.config.batchConfig!.flushInterval,\n      maxQueueSize: this.config.batchConfig!.maxQueueSize,\n      onFlush: async (items: BatchMemoryItem[]): Promise<BatchStoreResult[]> => {\n        return this.batchStoreInternal(items);\n      },\n    });\n    \n    log.info(\n      `Memory batching enabled (batch: ${this.config.batchConfig!.batchSize}, ` +\n      `interval: ${this.config.batchConfig!.flushInterval}ms)`\n    );\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * MODIFIED: Store memory (now uses batching if enabled)\n   */\n  async storeMemory(content: string, metadata?: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<StoreResult> {\n    this.ensureReady();\n    \n    // Use batching if enabled\n    if (this.memoryBatch) {\n      const result = await this.memoryBatch.push({ content, metadata });\n      return {\n        stored: result.stored,\n        episode_id: result.episode_id,\n        surprise: result.surprise,\n        is_novel: result.is_novel,\n        reason: result.reason,\n      };\n    }\n    \n    // Fallback to direct call\n    return this.request(\"store_memory\", { content, metadata });\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * MODIFIED: Store with embedding (uses batching if enabled)\n   */\n  async storeMemoryWithEmbedding(\n    content: string,\n    embedding: number[],\n    metadata?: Record<string, unknown>,\n  ): Promise<StoreResult> {\n    this.ensureReady();\n    \n    if (this.memoryBatch) {\n      const result = await this.memoryBatch.push({ content, embedding, metadata });\n      return {\n        stored: result.stored,\n        episode_id: result.episode_id,\n        surprise: result.surprise,\n        is_novel: result.is_novel,\n        reason: result.reason,\n      };\n    }\n    \n    return this.request(\"store_memory\", { content, embedding, metadata });\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * NEW: Internal batch store - sends to Python\n   */\n  private async batchStoreInternal(items: BatchMemoryItem[]): Promise<BatchStoreResult[]> {\n    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n      const id = String(++this.requestId);\n      \n      const callbacks = new Map<string, { resolve: Function; reject: Function }>();\n      \n      // Store callbacks for each item\n      this.requestCallbacks.set(id, {\n        resolve: (results: BatchStoreResult[]) => {\n          resolve(results);\n        },\n        reject: (error: Error) => {\n          reject(error);\n        },\n      });\n      \n      const request = JSON.stringify({\n        id,\n        method: \"batch_store_memory\",  // NEW Python method\n        params: {\n          items: items.map(item => ({\n            id: item.id,\n            content: item.content,\n            embedding: item.embedding,\n            metadata: item.metadata,\n          })),\n        },\n      }) + \"\\n\";\n      \n      log.debug(`[MCP→] Sending batch request ${id}: ${items.length} items`);\n      this.process?.stdin?.write(request);\n      \n      // Extended timeout for batch operations\n      const timeout = 120000; // 2 minutes for batches\n      setTimeout(() => {\n        if (this.requestCallbacks.has(id)) {\n          this.requestCallbacks.delete(id);\n          reject(new Error(`Batch store timeout after ${timeout / 1000}s`));\n        }\n      }, timeout);\n    });\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * MODIFIED: Process responses (handle batch results)\n   */\n  private processBuffer(): void {\n    const lines = this.buffer.split(\"\\n\");\n    this.buffer = lines.pop() || \"\";\n\n    for (const line of lines) {\n      if (!line.trim()) continue;\n\n      try {\n        const response = JSON.parse(line);\n        const callback = this.requestCallbacks.get(response.id);\n\n        if (callback) {\n          this.requestCallbacks.delete(response.id);\n          log.debug(`[MCP←] Received response for ${response.id}`);\n\n          if (response.error) {\n            callback.reject(new Error(response.error));\n          } else {\n            // Handle batch response format\n            if (Array.isArray(response.result)) {\n              callback.resolve(response.result);  // Batch result\n            } else {\n              callback.resolve(response.result);  // Single result\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      } catch (error) {\n        log.warn(\"Failed to parse response:\", line);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * MODIFIED: Stop with batch queue shutdown\n   */\n  async stop(): Promise<void> {\n    // Flush remaining memories before shutdown\n    if (this.memoryBatch) {\n      log.info(\"Flushing remaining memory batch...\");\n      await this.memoryBatch.shutdown();\n    }\n    \n    // ... existing stop logic ...\n  }\n  \n  /**\n   * NEW: Force flush batch queue\n   */\n  async flushBatch(): Promise<void> {\n    if (this.memoryBatch) {\n      await this.memoryBatch.flush();\n    }\n  }\n  \n  /**\n   * NEW: Get batch statistics\n   */\n  getBatchStats() {\n    return this.memoryBatch?.getStats() ?? null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Python MCP Server Addition\n\nThe Python `mcp_server.py` needs a new `batch_store_memory` method:\n\n```python\n# In mcp_server.py\n\ndef handle_batch_store_memory(params: dict) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Store multiple memories in a single batch.\"\"\"\n    items = params.get(\"items\", [])\n    results = []\n    \n    for item in items:\n        item_id = item[\"id\"]\n        content = item[\"content\"]\n        embedding = item.get(\"embedding\")  # Optional\n        metadata = item.get(\"metadata\", {})\n        \n        try:\n            # Use existing store logic\n            result = store_memory_internal(content, embedding, metadata)\n            results.append({\n                \"id\": item_id,\n                \"result\": result\n            })\n        except Exception as e:\n            results.append({\n                \"id\": item_id,\n                \"error\": str(e)\n            })\n    \n    return results\n\n# Register method\nMETHODS = {\n    \"store_memory\": handle_store_memory,\n    \"batch_store_memory\": handle_batch_store_memory,  # NEW\n    \"retrieve_memories\": handle_retrieve_memories,\n    \"consolidate_memories\": handle_consolidate_memories,\n    \"get_stats\": handle_get_stats,\n}\n```\n\n### 6. Edge Cases Analysis\n\n| Edge Case | Handling |\n|-----------|----------|\n| **Queue fills during burst** | Configurable `maxQueueSize` (default 100). Oldest items dropped with rejection. Caller gets error. |\n| **Python crashes mid-batch** | All pending callbacks rejected with error. Caller catches and logs. No memory leak (callbacks cleared). |\n| **Gateway restarts with queued** | Memory lost. Acceptable for episodic memory (non-critical). Could add `shutdown()` hook in gateway stop. |\n| **Partial batch failure** | Python returns per-item results. Failed items reject, succeeded items resolve. |\n| **Timeout during batch** | 2-minute batch timeout. All callbacks rejected. Queue cleared. |\n| **Ordering guarantees** | FIFO within batch. Batches processed in order. No interleaving. |\n| **Memory leak (callbacks)** | Callbacks deleted on: success, error, timeout, overflow drop. Map bounded by `maxQueueSize`. |\n\n### 7. Implementation Steps\n\n1. **Create `memory-batch-queue.ts`** - Batch queue class with debouncing\n2. **Modify `neuro-memory-bridge.ts`**:\n   - Add `MemoryBatchQueue` instance\n   - Add config options (`enableBatching`, `batchConfig`)\n   - Wrap `storeMemory()` to use batch queue\n   - Add `batchStoreInternal()` for Python IPC\n   - Update `processBuffer()` for batch responses\n   - Update `stop()` to flush queue\n3. **Modify Python `mcp_server.py`**:\n   - Add `batch_store_memory` method\n   - Register in method dispatch table\n4. **Add config schema** (`config/types.memory.ts`):\n   ```typescript\n   export type NeuroMemoryConfig = {\n     enabled: boolean;\n     agentPath?: string;\n     memorableTypes?: string[];\n     surpriseThreshold?: number;\n     // NEW\n     enableBatching?: boolean;\n     batchConfig?: {\n       batchSize?: number;      // default: 10\n       flushInterval?: number;  // default: 2000ms\n       maxQueueSize?: number;   // default: 100\n     };\n   };\n   ```\n5. **Add tests** (`neuro-memory-bridge.test.ts`):\n   - Batch queue behavior\n   - Overflow handling\n   - Graceful shutdown\n   - Python batch protocol\n\n### 8. Performance Estimate\n\n| Scenario | Before | After | Improvement |\n|----------|--------|-------|-------------|\n| 10 events burst | 10 × 300ms = 3s | 1 × 400ms = 0.4s | **7.5x faster** |\n| 50 events burst | 50 × 300ms = 15s | 5 × 400ms = 2s | **7.5x faster** |\n| 100 events burst | 100 × 300ms = 30s | 10 × 400ms = 4s | **7.5x faster** |\n\n**IPC Reduction**:\n- Before: N events → N JSON writes → N Python roundtrips\n- After: N events → ⌈N/batchSize⌉ JSON writes → ⌈N/batchSize⌉ roundtrips\n- **Reduction: 10x** (with batchSize=10)\n\n**Memory Overhead**:\n- Buffer: ~1KB per event × 100 max = 100KB\n- Callbacks: ~100 bytes × 100 = 10KB\n- **Total: ~110KB** (negligible)\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThe batch implementation should be added to `neuro-memory-bridge.ts` using a `MemoryBatchQueue` class (modeled after the existing `MetricsQueue`). The key changes:\n\n1. **TypeScript**: Add `memory-batch-queue.ts`, modify `neuro-memory-bridge.ts`\n2. **Python**: Add `batch_store_memory` method to `mcp_server.py`\n3. **Config**: Add batching options to `NeuroMemoryConfig`\n\nExpected improvement: **7-10x faster** memory storage during bursts, with **10x fewer IPC calls**."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zhipu","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":4202,"output":4607,"cacheRead":33152,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":41961,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1772964850520}}
